<title>SPAIN: Spain's Catalonia allotted 4.2 bln ptas at auction.</title>
<headline>Spain's Catalonia allotted 4.2 bln ptas at auction.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Catalan regional government the Generalitat de Catalunya said on Wednesday it allotted a total of 4.2 billion pesetas in five- and 10-year bonds at a public auction.</p>
<p>Yields fell versus the previous auction on November 20.</p>
<p>Results are as follows:</p>
<p>(in billions of pesetas)</p>
<p>ISSUE	   Yield  Pvs    Price   Pvs    Bid   Allocated</p>
<p>8.10% JULY 01 6.325  6.538  110.30 108.95  12.01 2.2</p>
<p>8.85% JULY 06 7.157  7.244  115.20 114.00  19.55 2.0</p>
<p>NOTE - In both cases new tranches of old issues were offered.</p>
<p>Moody's long-term debt rating for Generalitat de Catalunya is A1. At end-June 1996 the region's total debt was 1,018 billion pesetas of which 257 billion pesetas was in bonds.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom + 341 585 8340</p>
